; WHP-Drivers RTL8111E NDIS 3.1 Windows 95 RTM INF research skeleton.
; STATUS: DELIBERATELY NON-INSTALLABLE. DO NOT COPY TO WINDOWS\INF.
; This is not a driver package: the NDIS miniport image, PCIe resource
; handling, interrupt/DMA synchronization, and Win95 guest tests are missing.
; Candidate PCI family ID ONLY: PCI\VEN_10EC&DEV_8168
; This ID is shared across RTL8168/RTL8111 chip revisions. It does NOT
; prove RTL8111E and is NOT an enabled device/model mapping below.
; Before activation verify exact vendor/device/revision/subsystem ID on
; the target computer and successful PCI bridge enumeration in Win95 RTM.
;
; HISTORICAL INSTALLATION CHECKLIST (comments only, NEVER active):
; - Bind a verified PCI model to a checked .ndi install section.
; - Audit NDIS 3.x miniport service loading (DevLoader / DeviceVxDs).
; - Audit NDI interface direction: UpperRange=ndis3; LowerRange=ethernet.
; - Audit NDI\\Install ndis3 registration, SourceDisks*, CopyFiles,
;   DestinationDirs, and copied .SYS file against a verified DDK witness.
; - Compare Windows 95 RTM NET*.INF samples; no NT .Services section.
; - Run an isolated Windows 95 RTM VM test before ever binding real NIC.

[Version]
Signature="$CHICAGO$"
Class=Net
Provider=%WHP%

[Manufacturer]
%WHP%=WHP.RTL8111E

[WHP.RTL8111E]
; Intentionally empty: no model or PCI binding while driver is incomplete.

[Strings]
WHP="WHP-Drivers (research only)"
RTL8111E="Realtek RTL8111E Ethernet (research, not installable)"
